{% set name = entry.name %}
Loupe's settings layout. {{ entry.summary }}

```jsx
<{{ name }}
  title="Project settings"
  description="Rename the project, or change how it works."
  navLabel="Project settings"
  items={[
    { label: 'General', href: '#', active: true },
    { label: 'Columns', href: '#' },
  ]}
>
  <section className="lp-settings-panel-card">
    <h2 className="lp-section-title">General</h2>
  </section>
</{{ name }}>
```

Pass one item for each section and mark the open one `active`. Put each panel of the open section in a `lp-settings-panel-card` section inside the content. Pass `columns` for a page whose content needs its own column width.

Titles are sentence case and never end in a full stop. The component emits the real `{{ entry.rootClass }}` classes of the app.
